@startuml error_flow_oauth_failure

title COOKie MVP - OAuth Provider Failure Handling Flow\nYandex ID & VK ID Error Scenarios

actor "User" as User
participant "Frontend\n(Next.js)" as Frontend
participant "Auth Controller\n(Backend)" as Controller
participant "OAuth Service" as OAuthService
cloud "Yandex ID\n(oauth.yandex.ru)" as Yandex
cloud "VK ID\n(oauth.vk.com)" as VK
database "PostgreSQL\nusers table" as DB
database "Redis\nblacklist" as Redis
participant "Serilog\nLogger" as Logger
participant "Sentry\nMonitoring" as Sentry

== Scenario 1: OAuth Provider Timeout ==

User -> Frontend: Click "Login with Yandex"
Frontend -> Controller: GET /api/v1/auth/oauth/yandex?\nredirect_uri=https://cookie.com/auth/callback
activate Controller

Controller -> OAuthService: exchange_code(authorization_code)
activate OAuthService

OAuthService -> Yandex: POST https://oauth.yandex.ru/token\n{\n  grant_type: "authorization_code",\n  code: "abc123",\n  client_id: "...",\n  client_secret: "..."\n}\n(timeout: 10 seconds)
activate Yandex

Yandex -> Yandex: Processing...\n(server overloaded)

note over Yandex
  No response within 10 seconds
end note

Yandex --> OAuthService: Timeout\n(no response)
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "OAuth token exchange timeout",\n  provider: "yandex",\n  timeout_ms: 10000,\n  attempt: 1\n)

OAuthService -> OAuthService: Retry attempt 1\n(delay: 2 seconds)

OAuthService -> Yandex: POST https://oauth.yandex.ru/token\n(retry)
activate Yandex

Yandex --> OAuthService: Timeout again
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> OAuthService: Retry attempt 2\n(delay: 4 seconds)

OAuthService -> Yandex: POST https://oauth.yandex.ru/token\n(final retry)
activate Yandex

Yandex --> OAuthService: Timeout\n(3 retries exhausted)
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> Logger: Log.Error(\n  "OAuth provider timeout after 3 retries",\n  provider: "yandex",\n  total_time_ms: 22000\n)

OAuthService -> Sentry: CaptureException(\n  OAuthProviderTimeoutException,\n  tags: { provider: "yandex" }\n)

OAuthService --> Controller: Throw OAuthProviderUnavailableException(\n  provider: "yandex",\n  reason: "timeout"\n)
deactivate OAuthService

Controller --> Frontend: 302 Redirect to:\nhttps://cookie.com/auth/callback?\n  error=provider_unavailable&\n  provider=yandex&\n  message=Yandex+ID+temporarily+unavailable
deactivate Controller

Frontend -> Frontend: Parse error from callback URL

Frontend --> User: Show error screen:\n"Yandex ID temporarily unavailable.\nPlease try again later or\nregister with email."\n\n[Try Again] [Register with Email]

== Scenario 2: Invalid Authorization Code ==

User -> Frontend: OAuth callback with code
Frontend -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/oauth/yandex/callback\n{"code": "expired_or_invalid_code"}
activate Controller

Controller -> OAuthService: exchange_code("expired_or_invalid_code")
activate OAuthService

OAuthService -> Yandex: POST https://oauth.yandex.ru/token\n{"code": "expired_or_invalid_code", ...}
activate Yandex

Yandex --> OAuthService: 400 Bad Request\n{\n  "error": "invalid_grant",\n  "error_description": "Code has expired"\n}
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "OAuth invalid grant",\n  provider: "yandex",\n  error: "invalid_grant",\n  description: "Code has expired"\n)

OAuthService --> Controller: Throw OAuthInvalidGrantException(\n  provider: "yandex",\n  reason: "Code has expired"\n)
deactivate OAuthService

Controller --> Frontend: 302 Redirect to:\nhttps://cookie.com/auth/callback?\n  error=invalid_code&\n  provider=yandex
deactivate Controller

Frontend -> Frontend: Clear any stale OAuth state

Frontend --> User: Show error:\n"Authentication session expired.\nPlease try logging in again."\n\n[Login with Yandex] [Login with VK]

== Scenario 3: OAuth Provider Returns Error ==

User -> Frontend: Click "Login with VK"
Frontend -> User: Redirect to VK authorization page

User -> VK: User denies permission\nor closes popup

VK --> Frontend: Redirect callback with error:\n/auth/callback?\n  error=access_denied&\n  error_description=The+user+denied+access

Frontend -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/oauth/vk/callback\n{"error": "access_denied"}
activate Controller

Controller -> Controller: Detect error parameter\nin callback

Controller -> Logger: Log.Information(\n  "OAuth permission denied by user",\n  provider: "vk",\n  error: "access_denied"\n)

Controller --> Frontend: 302 Redirect to:\nhttps://cookie.com/login?\n  error=oauth_denied&\n  provider=vk
deactivate Controller

Frontend --> User: Show message:\n"VK login was cancelled.\nYou can try again or use\nanother login method."\n\n[Login with VK] [Login with Yandex] [Register with Email]

== Scenario 4: User Profile Fetch Failure ==

User -> Frontend: OAuth callback (code received)
Frontend -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/oauth/yandex/callback\n{"code": "valid_code_123"}
activate Controller

Controller -> OAuthService: exchange_code("valid_code_123")
activate OAuthService

OAuthService -> Yandex: POST https://oauth.yandex.ru/token
activate Yandex
Yandex --> OAuthService: 200 OK\n{"access_token": "ya_token_xyz"}
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> Yandex: GET https://login.yandex.ru/info?\nformat=json\nAuthorization: OAuth ya_token_xyz
activate Yandex

Yandex --> OAuthService: 500 Internal Server Error\n(Yandex profile service down)
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> OAuthService: Retry fetching profile\n(2 retries, 1s delay)

OAuthService -> Yandex: GET https://login.yandex.ru/info
activate Yandex
Yandex --> OAuthService: 500 Error (still down)
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> Logger: Log.Error(\n  "OAuth profile fetch failed",\n  provider: "yandex",\n  error: "500 Internal Server Error",\n  had_valid_token: true\n)

OAuthService -> Sentry: CaptureException(\n  OAuthProfileFetchException,\n  context: { token_valid: true }\n)

OAuthService --> Controller: Throw OAuthProfileFetchException(\n  "Could not retrieve user profile"\n)
deactivate OAuthService

Controller --> Frontend: 302 Redirect to:\nhttps://cookie.com/auth/callback?\n  error=profile_unavailable&\n  provider=yandex
deactivate Controller

Frontend --> User: Show error:\n"Could not retrieve your Yandex profile.\nPlease try again in a few minutes."\n\n[Try Again] [Register with Email]

== Scenario 5: Account Linking Conflict ==

User -> Frontend: Login with Yandex (first time)
Frontend -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/oauth/yandex/callback\n{"code": "valid_code"}
activate Controller

Controller -> OAuthService: authenticate_oauth(provider, code)
activate OAuthService

OAuthService -> Yandex: Exchange code + fetch profile
activate Yandex
Yandex --> OAuthService: Profile:\n{\n  "id": "yandex-123",\n  "default_email": "user@mail.ru",\n  "first_name": "Ivan"\n}
deactivate Yandex

OAuthService -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE email = 'user@mail.ru'
activate DB
DB --> OAuthService: User found:\n{\n  id: "user-uuid-1",\n  email: "user@mail.ru",\n  oauth_provider: "vk",\n  oauth_id: "vk-456"\n}
deactivate DB

OAuthService -> OAuthService: Conflict detected:\nEmail 'user@mail.ru' already registered\nvia VK OAuth (different provider)

OAuthService -> Logger: Log.Information(\n  "OAuth account linking conflict",\n  email: sha256("user@mail.ru"),\n  existing_provider: "vk",\n  new_provider: "yandex"\n)

alt Auto-Link: Same Email, Link Both Providers
  OAuthService -> DB: UPDATE users SET\n  oauth_providers = oauth_providers || \n  '{"yandex": {"id": "yandex-123"}}'\nWHERE id = 'user-uuid-1'
  activate DB
  DB --> OAuthService: Updated (both providers linked)
  deactivate DB

  OAuthService -> OAuthService: Generate JWT tokens\nfor existing user

  OAuthService --> Controller: AuthResult {\n  user: {id: "user-uuid-1"},\n  access_token: "jwt...",\n  refresh_token: "rt...",\n  linked_provider: "yandex"\n}
  deactivate OAuthService

  Controller --> Frontend: 302 Redirect to:\nhttps://cookie.com/auth/callback?\n  token=jwt...&\n  linked=yandex&\n  message=Account+linked+with+Yandex

  Frontend --> User: "Welcome back, Ivan!\nYour Yandex account has been\nlinked to your existing account."
  deactivate Controller

else Conflict: Email Exists with Password Auth
  OAuthService -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE email = 'user@mail.ru'
  activate DB
  DB --> OAuthService: User found:\n{\n  id: "user-uuid-1",\n  email: "user@mail.ru",\n  password_hash: "$2b$...",\n  oauth_provider: null\n}
  deactivate DB

  OAuthService -> Logger: Log.Information(\n  "OAuth conflict with password account",\n  email_hash: sha256("user@mail.ru"),\n  provider: "yandex"\n)

  OAuthService --> Controller: Throw AccountLinkingConflictException(\n  "Email registered with password auth"\n)
  deactivate OAuthService

  Controller --> Frontend: 302 Redirect to:\nhttps://cookie.com/auth/callback?\n  error=account_exists&\n  provider=yandex&\n  auth_method=password
  deactivate Controller

  Frontend --> User: "An account with this email already exists.\nPlease login with your password,\nthen link Yandex in settings."\n\n[Login with Password] [Forgot Password?]
end

== Scenario 6: VK-Specific Error (API Version) ==

User -> Frontend: Login with VK
Frontend -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/oauth/vk/callback\n{"code": "vk_code"}
activate Controller

Controller -> OAuthService: exchange_code("vk_code")
activate OAuthService

OAuthService -> VK: POST https://oauth.vk.com/access_token
activate VK
VK --> OAuthService: 200 OK\n{"access_token": "vk_token", "user_id": 12345}
deactivate VK

OAuthService -> VK: GET https://api.vk.com/method/users.get?\n  user_ids=12345&\n  fields=photo_200,email&\n  v=5.131&\n  access_token=vk_token
activate VK

VK --> OAuthService: 200 OK\n{\n  "error": {\n    "error_code": 5,\n    "error_msg": "User authorization failed: invalid access_token"\n  }\n}
deactivate VK

OAuthService -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "VK API error",\n  error_code: 5,\n  error_msg: "invalid access_token",\n  provider: "vk"\n)

OAuthService -> OAuthService: Map VK error code:\n- 5: invalid token → retry auth\n- 6: rate limit → wait and retry\n- 10: internal error → retry\n- 14: captcha needed → fail\n- 17: validation needed → fail

OAuthService --> Controller: Throw OAuthTokenInvalidException(\n  provider: "vk",\n  reason: "Token rejected by VK API"\n)
deactivate OAuthService

Controller --> Frontend: 302 Redirect to:\nhttps://cookie.com/auth/callback?\n  error=token_invalid&\n  provider=vk
deactivate Controller

Frontend --> User: "VK authentication failed.\nPlease try again."\n\n[Try Again] [Login with Yandex] [Register with Email]

== OAuth Retry Strategy ==

note over OAuthService, Yandex
  **OAuth Retry Policy:**

  **Token Exchange (POST /token):**
  - Max retries: 2
  - Delay: 2s, 4s (exponential)
  - Timeout per attempt: 10 seconds
  - Retryable: timeout, 5xx errors
  - Non-retryable: 400, 401, 403

  **Profile Fetch (GET /info):**
  - Max retries: 2
  - Delay: 1s, 2s
  - Timeout per attempt: 5 seconds
  - Retryable: timeout, 5xx errors
  - Non-retryable: 401, 403, 404

  **Account Linking Strategy:**
  - Same email + different OAuth → auto-link
  - Same email + password auth → prompt login
  - New email → create new account
  - Same provider + same ID → login existing

  **Security Considerations:**
  - State parameter for CSRF protection
  - Nonce verification (Yandex)
  - Token exchange within 5 minutes of code
  - Never log access tokens (only hashes)
  - Clear OAuth state after use
end note

== Provider-Specific Error Codes ==

note over Yandex, VK
  **Yandex ID Error Codes:**
  - invalid_grant: Code expired or used
  - invalid_client: Wrong client_id/secret
  - unauthorized_client: App not approved
  - invalid_scope: Requested scope denied
  - server_error: Yandex internal error

  **VK ID Error Codes:**
  - 5: Invalid access token
  - 6: Too many requests (rate limit)
  - 10: Internal server error
  - 14: Captcha required
  - 15: Access denied
  - 17: Validation required (2FA)
  - 29: Rate limit reached

  **Common Handling:**
  - Log all provider errors with context
  - Map to user-friendly messages
  - Never expose provider details to user
  - Offer alternative auth methods
end note

